    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: ee50099d8a70c37b2edc6e12ab5a3b44a6b4b63b -->\n**Ready for the maintainer to merge** (review of head ee50099, trial-merged with current main 5a37b737; the PR is a draft and I left that as it is).\n\n**What looks good**\n- Refresh check: the merged tree differs from origin/main only in the PR's own 33 files (no main-side file dropped or reverted). `PROJECT_VERSION` is 60 in `project/file.rs`, with the doc/comment in `project/mod.rs` and the decision note agreeing. The v59 ladder rung from #1056 (`fidelity_migrate::settle`) is intact and the v59 -> v60 note sits beside it in `apply.rs`.\n- Round trip: `program` is `skip_serializing_if` none, so a document that states nothing writes no key; a stated number/comment round-trips (`the_program_info_round_trips_and_an_older_file_states_none`). A file older than v60 steps up with nothing stated and overwrites a stale in-memory value. A hand-edited bad value is refused as a corrupt file before any world write, by the same rules `SetProgramInfo` runs.\n- Prime Directive: number 1..=9999 and comment (<=40 printable ASCII, no `( ) % ; *`) refused by name at command creation. `program_id` refuses a per-op count past O9999 rather than wrapping. `fanuc.cps` no longer clamps a bad number onto 9999 - it throws by name. SINUMERIK refuses a program name its rules forbid instead of renaming it. No unwrap/expect/panic in the new non-test code.\n- Undoable `SetProgramInfo` (invert restores prev), with the `set_program` MCP tool. Layering and schema placement are right (`ProgramInfo` in `schema.rs`). Post-side `ProgramId` lives in camcraft-post. Provenance lines present, no new crate dependency lines.\n- The hand-resolved `mcp/setup_tools.rs`, `posting.rs`, `posting_mounts.rs`, `posting_per_op.rs` read correctly: all three post paths (single, per-mount, per-op) now take the id from `document_program_id`.\n\n**Local results (merged with main)**\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| post: lib + post_engine, script_{fanuc,fanuc_lathe,haas,heidenhain,mazak,sinumerik,tormach}, fanuc_post, heidenhain_block_form, recorded_streams, comment_escape | all pass (39+33+11+15+11+11+11+11+12+5+12+3) |\n| app: lib 154, program_info 9, project_roundtrip 73, mcp_setup 9, mcp 19, posting 17, per_op_files 9, setup_mounts_post 8, program_comments 4, setup_post_options 10, commands_undo 30, tormach_post 10 | all pass |\n| ui lib (from crates/ui) | 643 passed, 5 ignored |\n| clippy -D warnings, post + app + ui, all targets | clean |\n\n**Requested before merge**: none.\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n- The round-trip test steps up from a v58 file; a literal v59 fixture would pin the \"main's v59 still loads\" claim more directly. v59 goes through the same ladder, and I did not find a gap.\n- `PROJECT_VERSION` bump is a format change; the title is `feat(post)` and the changelog/Fixes lines should stay as the author wrote them (no CHANGELOG edit in the diff, good).\n- Several `.cps` files and `posting_program.rs` are fine on size; no snapshot PNG or golden changes.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
